{
  "comment": "Spatial navigation scenarios on spatnav.js in an 800 x 600 viewport: Chrome with --enable-spatial-navigation, weft with WEFT_PAGE_SPATIAL_NAVIGATION. A step presses a key (down, its text when it has one, up), holds or releases one, clicks an element's centre, focuses or blurs by script. keys: key, code, Windows virtual key and the text the key types (Enter's '\\r' types no text in weft: its keypress comes from its keydown). chrome-results.json is what Chrome did (tools/browser_spatial_navigation_reference.mjs); tests/spatial_navigation_tests.cpp replays the steps in a View and compares.",
  "width": 800,
  "height": 600,
  "keys": {
    "Tab": {"key": "Tab", "code": "Tab", "vk": 9},
    "Enter": {"key": "Enter", "code": "Enter", "vk": 13, "text": "\r"},
    "Escape": {"key": "Escape", "code": "Escape", "vk": 27},
    "ArrowUp": {"key": "ArrowUp", "code": "ArrowUp", "vk": 38},
    "ArrowDown": {"key": "ArrowDown", "code": "ArrowDown", "vk": 40},
    "ArrowLeft": {"key": "ArrowLeft", "code": "ArrowLeft", "vk": 37},
    "ArrowRight": {"key": "ArrowRight", "code": "ArrowRight", "vk": 39}
  },
